                <pb facs="0841" n="741" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg741"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5431/97: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Williamson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-11-15T13:00:00+01:00">November 15, 1934—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 17—9:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. Department’s 67, November 14, 7 p.m. Swiss Department of Public Economy has
                    already on more than one occasion strongly advised against Swiss business
                    interests making proposed <hi rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> on December 17.
                    While it of course cannot prevent departure to the United States of Swiss
                    citizens it will reiterate its position through official and semiofficial bodies
                    such as Chambers of Commerce.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Williamson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
